{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0247","billNumberShort":"H.B. 247","billNumberLong":"HB0247S05","fileNumber":"2026FL0962","shortTitle":"Great Salt Lake Related Amendments","currentSubVersion":"5","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"WARDR","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Ward, Raymond P.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"SANDASD","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Sandall, Scott D.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses activities that are related to the Great Salt Lake.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>directs revenue generated by the brine shrimp royalty tax to the Sovereign Lands Management Account instead of the Species Protection Account under certain circumstances;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the rate of the brine shrimp royalty tax;<hr><ltbullet>modifies a provision concerning calculation of severance tax related to certain Great Salt Lake extraction operators;<hr><ltbullet>addresses the timing of certification of information related to severance taxes and certain Great Salt Lake extraction operators;<hr><ltbullet>provides for the deposit of proceeds from a judgment, settlement, or compromise into the Sovereign Lands Management Account;<hr><ltbullet>provides for how the revenue in the Sovereign Lands Management Account is to be spent; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Patricia Owen","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"BVLGSNYIUH","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-13 15:29:19.487","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and G